<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rodez</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Segodunum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rodez is a town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aveyron">Aveyron</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>, on a hill above the Aveyron River. As Segodunum it was the chief town of the Gallic Ruteni, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the seat of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> and of the counts of Rodez. Its red sandstone Gothic cathedral dominates the town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rodez.jpg" alt="Rodez" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kallerna · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rodez_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
